9:["$","$L1e",null,{"faqItems":[{"q":"What conditions does an ENT specialist treat?","a":"An ENT specialist diagnoses and treats conditions related to the ear, nose, throat, sinus, hearing, allergies, breathing, voice, snoring, sleep-related airway issues, and selected head & neck disorders."},{"q":"When should I consult an ENT specialist?","a":"If symptoms are persistent, recurrent, worsening, affecting sleep, hearing, breathing, swallowing, or daily quality of life, specialist evaluation is recommended."},{"q":"Are all ENT conditions surgical?","a":"No. Many ENT conditions are treated successfully through medication, allergy management, lifestyle adjustments, or minimally invasive therapies. Surgery is recommended only when clinically necessary."},{"q":"Can allergies cause sinus and breathing problems?","a":"Yes. Allergies may lead to chronic nasal inflammation, blocked nose, sinus congestion, snoring, and recurrent ENT symptoms."}]}]
